    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "After Mikhail's warning, Chef Barinov storms toward the back room to punish Senya and Fedya, only to mistake Mikhail and a guest's pet monkey for his cooks. Listen to the Russian scene.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Даже не смей так говорить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "У тебя не всё нормально.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не сметь от меня закрываться!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я вас всех сегодня уволю!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ах ты, макака такая!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Извини, я не так подумал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Это вам не просто макака.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Сегодня действует всё меню ресторана.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Гости ждут заказ с сегодняшнего дня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я просто ненавижу это правило.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Шеф, что сейчас здесь было?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А что, вкусный банан?",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Даже не смей так говорить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do not even dare to say that.' Notice how Russian expresses 'even' and 'to speak' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "У тебя не всё нормально.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Not everything is fine with you.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'at' and finishing on 'normally'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не сметь от меня закрываться!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do not dare lock yourselves in from me!' An emphatic spoken line centered on the verb meaning 'to dare'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я вас всех сегодня уволю!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will fire all of you today!' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'I' and finishing on 'will fire'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ах ты, макака такая!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Oh, you little macaque monkey!' Chef Barinov brings out the contrast between 'ah' and 'you' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Извини, я не так подумал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Sorry, I thought the wrong thing.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'sorry' and finishing on 'to think'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Это вам не просто макака.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is not just a monkey to you.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'this' and finishing on 'macaque monkey'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Сегодня действует всё меню ресторана.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Today the entire restaurant menu is active.' Mikhail anchors the line on 'tonight', while 'restaurant' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Гости ждут заказ с сегодняшнего дня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Guests are waiting for orders starting today.' The grammar packs 'guests' and 'day' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я просто ненавижу это правило.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I simply hate this rule.' The meaning hinges on 'I' working together with 'rule' in spoken Russian. Senya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Шеф, что сейчас здесь было?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Chef, what just happened here?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'Chef Barinov' before landing on 'was'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А что, вкусный банан?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well, is it a tasty banana?' The meaning hinges on 'and' working together with 'banana' in spoken Russian. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
